# Threat Model Mapping: HyperFleet Auth & Tenancy


```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph Threats
        T1(No credential, or unknown issuer token)
        T2(Valid SA token from unlisted service account)
        T3(Human token without required tenant claim)
        T4(Client forges tenant headers via Envoy)
        T5(Pod bypasses Envoy and calls API without credential)
        T6(Pod forges tenant headers using its own wristband)
        T7(Token read in transit inside the cluster)
        T8(Envoy pointed at impostor Authorino/API)
    end

    subgraph Mitigation Controls
        C1[Authorino denies at gateway]
        C2[Exact allow-list in TokenReview]
        C3[Required-claim rule at gateway]
        C4[Envoy early header mutation strips them]
        C5[API requires wristband / NetworkPolicy]
        C6[Tenancy sourced from signed wristband claims]
        C7[TLS on both in-cluster hops]
        C8[CA validation on transport sockets]
    end

    subgraph Required Mode
        M_Edge[Mode: edge]
        M_EdgeAPI[Mode: edge+api]
        M_TLS[Tickets: 1648 and 1635]
    end

    T1 -->|Prevented by| C1 --> M_Edge
    T2 -->|Prevented by| C2 --> M_Edge
    T3 -->|Prevented by| C3 --> M_Edge
    T4 -->|Prevented by| C4 --> M_Edge
    T5 -->|Prevented by| C5 --> M_EdgeAPI
    T6 -->|Prevented by| C6 --> M_EdgeAPI
    T7 -->|Prevented by| C7 --> M_TLS
    T8 -->|Prevented by| C8 --> M_TLS
    
    classDef threat fill:#ffebee,stroke:#ff5252,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef control fill:#e8f5e9,stroke:#4caf50,stroke-width:2px;
    classDef mode fill:#e3f2fd,stroke:#2196f3,stroke-width:2px;
    
    class T1,T2,T3,T4,T5,T6,T7,T8 threat;
    class C1,C2,C3,C4,C5,C6,C7,C8 control;
    class M_Edge,M_EdgeAPI,M_TLS mode;
